{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000015"], "form": "structure", "observation": {"citations": [{"quote": "So first thing I'll make sure like I have the right project and folder setup. And second I make sure I write the reusable components, reusable functions and components that are really required for the project. Third thing I make sure all the security aspects are taken care. Fourth I make sure performance is taken care. Fifth I make sure there is no tech theft.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000015"}], "text": "Five-point list format is used to outline sequential steps for starting a new development project, with additional focus points beyond the initial three items requested."}, "purpose": null, "speaker_id": "0", "title": "Sequential steps for project setup", "topic": "front_end_development"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:expression:f1465b879d7544e9", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "expression", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "Sequential steps for project setup", "topic": "front_end_development", "topic_slug": "front_end_development"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000037"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "self_report", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "Okay. So quite a few different ways that I can use to I can I can basically work to optimize the application. Probably one is lazy loading. Another one is efficiently using the network call.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000037"}], "text": "Various techniques for optimizing a React application include lazy loading, efficiently using network calls, optimally using resources, using right branching strategies, and dynamic loading where content is loaded only on a required basis."}, "title": "React application optimization techniques", "topic": "ReactJS optimization"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:knowledge:83188a5075a354dc", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "React application optimization techniques", "topic": "ReactJS optimization", "topic_slug": "reactjs-optimization"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000040"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "claim", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "You not just that in fact, if you wanted to assess it fully and give you an assessment sort of a format in a tabular form what is correct, what is wrong, what to improve, Chat GPT will give you that.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000040"}], "text": "Chat GPT can be used as a free tool to conduct mock interviews, providing feedback in a tabular format with assessments of what is correct, wrong, and what could be improved."}, "title": "Using Chat GPT for mock interviews", "topic": "AI tools for mock interviews"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:knowledge:7a30171273672d8a", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "Using Chat GPT for mock interviews", "topic": "AI tools for mock interviews", "topic_slug": "ai-tools-for-mock-interviews"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000049"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "self_report", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "So state is a state is nothing but a memory of a component whenever as long as the component is live the state will be live. Whereas the prop is something nothing but a property that you pass to a component. So depending on it's more like you passing a argument to a function that has prop state is a memory of a component that's the difference.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000049"}], "text": "State is like the memory of a component, live as long as the component is live; props are like arguments passed to a function, serving as properties conveyed to a component."}, "title": "Comparison between state and props in React", "topic": "ReactJS theory"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:knowledge:8fff1c86939faf37", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "Comparison between state and props in React", "topic": "ReactJS theory", "topic_slug": "reactjs-theory"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"constraints": [], "context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000050"], "exceptions": [], "goal": null, "kind": "offering", "prerequisites": [], "steps": [], "summary": {"citations": [{"quote": "State is data that lives inside a component itself. It can change over time, and it's up to the component to manage those changes. Props, on the other hand, are used to pass data into a component from its parent.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000050"}], "text": "State is data that lives inside a component and can change over time; it's managed by the component. Props are data passed into a component from its parent, akin to read-only snapshots, and cannot be changed from within the component."}, "title": "State and props detailed explanation in React", "topic": "ReactJS theory"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:knowledge:b278534647c64f80", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "knowledge", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "State and props detailed explanation in React", "topic": "ReactJS theory", "topic_slug": "reactjs-theory"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000035", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000036", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000037", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000038", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000039"], "cue": {"citations": [{"quote": "Sure. How would you optimize performance in a React application?", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000036"}], "text": "The interviewer asks: 'How would you optimize performance in a React application?'"}, "diagnosis": null, "kind": "recorded_exchange", "outcome": null, "rationale": null, "response": {"citations": [{"quote": "Okay. So quite a few different ways that I can use to I can I can basically work to optimize the application. Probably one is lazy loading.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000037"}], "text": "Vasanth lists several optimization techniques: lazy loading, efficiently using network calls, optimally using resources, right branching strategies, dynamic loading where content is loaded only as needed."}, "situation": {"citations": [{"quote": "I did not fully get the question, Chachipati. Can you please repeat it?", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000035"}], "text": "Vasanth participates in a mock interview where the interviewer asks about optimizing performance in a React application."}, "speaker_id": "0", "strategy": null, "title": "Optimize React performance", "topic": "ReactJS optimization"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:cases:a41447561e7fdebe", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "cases", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "Optimize React performance", "topic": "ReactJS optimization", "topic_slug": "reactjs-optimization"}
{"author": "careerwithvasanth", "category": "youtube", "content": {"context_unit_ids": ["youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000043", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000044", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000045", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000046", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000047", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000048", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000049", "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000050"], "cue": {"citations": [{"quote": "Can you explain the difference between state and props in React?", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000046"}], "text": "Gemini asks Vasanth to explain the difference between state and props in React."}, "diagnosis": null, "kind": "recorded_exchange", "outcome": {"citations": [{"quote": "That's partially correct, Vasant. You're right that state and props are different, but let's be more specific.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000050"}], "text": "Gemini provides feedback, noting Vasanth's partial correctness and offering a more specific explanation about state and props."}, "rationale": null, "response": {"citations": [{"quote": "So state is a state is nothing but a memory of a component whenever as long as the component is live the state will be live. Whereas the prop is something nothing but a property that you pass to a component.", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000049"}], "text": "Vasanth answers that state is the memory of a component, while props are properties passed to a component, similar to arguments to a function."}, "situation": {"citations": [{"quote": "Hey hey Jamina, can we actually get started with a mock interview for three year experience front end developer using React JS?", "unit_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:u000045"}], "text": "Vasanth initiates a mock interview with Gemini focused on a front-end developer with ReactJS experience."}, "speaker_id": "0", "strategy": null, "title": "Mock interview with Gemini for React JS", "topic": "AI tools for mock interviews"}, "content_hash": "7642d758c7eef9e533a57d022c423f90efc4ff13ef92e2de05436657cb4baf6a", "external_status": "not_checked", "extraction_scope": "source_excerpt", "id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86:cases:88c7dd7a58ee1243", "metadata_hash": "77241a8f376208f180d70fdb6d351bd2ca52eb793268357d061b672c739643ed", "product": "cases", "published_at": "2025-02-20", "semantic_status": "not_reviewed", "source_format": "transcript", "source_hash": "a0b67cac56932280fb8e93b7c2398fae6b0b57022ccbe5a69f2386cd61960da3", "source_id": "youtube-video-2025-02-20-top-free-ai-mock-interview-tools-you-must-try-in-2025-iggkmk-61e01dee86", "source_url": "https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=iGGkmKN8ilw", "title": "Mock interview with Gemini for React JS", "topic": "AI tools for mock interviews", "topic_slug": "ai-tools-for-mock-interviews"}
